Re-deriving: \((n+36)^2 - k^2 = 1296\), so \((n+36-k)(n+36+k)=1296\). Both factors must be positive even divisors. Checking even factor pairs \(a \le b\), \(ab=1296\), I previously missed the pair \((8,162)\), which gives \(n = \frac{8+162}{2}-36 = 49\). Indeed \(49^2+72\cdot49 = 5929 = 77^2\).

Valid positive \(n\): 289, 128, 75, 49, 24, 9, 3. Sum \(= 577\). The earlier sum omitted 49.

