The individual counts were right: 81 for the radius-5 circle and 29 for the radius-3 circle. But the overlap claim was wrong: having no common boundary lattice point does not imply the disks have no common lattice points.

Using \(u=x-4,\ v=y-3\), the small disk is \(u^2+v^2\le 9\). Testing those 29 points in \(x^2+y^2\le25\) gives 13 overlaps. So the union count is \(81+29-13=97\).

